response:
 How can I do that? If you want to iterate through all rows, then there is no need to use a For Loop. The for loop is the most commonly used loop to iterate through the rows of the dataset. Here is an example:

for(i in 1:length(data) ){
data[i, ]
}

Note: The 1:length(data) means that you are iterating over the rows from the first row to the last row of the dataset.
